Chapter: CheckVmDifferentialScript

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Shell chapter ShellTypes
  cites Shell chapter ShellBuild
  cites Shell chapter Pipeline
  cites Shell chapter PowerShellEmit

 We say:

 THE TWENTY-SECOND GENERATOR ON THE PIPELINE MODEL (PipelineModel.md), and the
 DEGENERATE CASE: this script's assembly is one `ScSequence`, so the pipeline
 below carries exactly one stage. Splitting the raw body into several would put
 each in its own `ScSequence` and gain a blank line per boundary, which is
 drift, so the structure stays as the script's own.

 THE RETURN HERE IS THE VERDICT LIST, NOT THE STAGES. Six exits live inside raw
 payloads and no walk of the body would find any of them, and two of the six
 are ZEROS that mean opposite things: a machine with one VM host SKIPS and
 reports success, and two hosts agreeing byte for byte also reports success. A
 caller gating on this script's exit code cannot tell the check from its own
 absence. The emitted script is byte-identical to the one that shipped before
 the migration.

Section: Parameters

  vmdiff-params : List ShellParam = [sh-param-default "Src" SptString (SeLit ""), sh-param-default "Kernel" SptString (SeLit ""), sh-switch "Quiet"]

Section: S01 -- Body

  s01 : List ShellCmd = [ScSetStrictMode, ScSetErrorStop, ScBlank, ScRaw "# Why this check exists, and it is trust rather than correctness.", ScRaw "#", ScRaw "# QEMU is a third-party binary and its Authenticode signature cannot tell a", ScRaw "# good build from a hostile one. The publisher's signing certificate expired", ScRaw "# 2023-09-12 and the binaries are still signed with it, so verification", ScRaw "# returns the same failure whether or not that key is still in the", ScRaw "# publisher's hands. Revocation is the mechanism that would normally carry", ScRaw "# the news, and there is nothing left to revoke. A check that answers", ScRaw "# identically in both worlds carries no information.", ScRaw "#", ScRaw "# Two independent VM hosts agreeing on the output byte for byte does carry", ScRaw "# information. codex-vm is ours and QEMU is theirs; they share no code, no", ScRaw "# accelerator and no author. A QEMU altered to corrupt compiler output has to", ScRaw "# reproduce the exact bytes our own hypervisor produces from the same source", ScRaw "# on the same machine.", ScRaw "#", ScRaw "# This is not a proof. It is one sample, and it does not catch an attacker", ScRaw "# who corrupts only a seed rebuild. It is an assertion with a runner, which", ScRaw "# is more than the certificate has ever been.", ScRaw "#", ScRaw "# Exit 0 on match, and 0 on a skip: a machine with only one host is the", ScRaw "# normal case, not a failure. Exit 1 on a byte mismatch, which is the whole", ScRaw "# reason the script exists.", ScBlank, ScRaw "$Repo = (Resolve-Path (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot '..')).Path", ScRaw ". (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'vm-config.ps1')", ScBlank, ScRaw "if (-not $Src) { $Src = Join-Path $Repo 'codex' 'test' 'act-let-scope.codex' }", ScRaw "if (-not $Kernel) { $Kernel = Join-Path $Repo 'seed' 'Codex.cdx' }", ScBlank, ScRaw "# Host discovery in vm-config honours CODEX_VM_HOST, which this script sets", ScRaw "# per arm. Ask the filesystem instead so the skip decision is about what is", ScRaw "# installed rather than about how the last caller was configured.", ScRaw "$codexVmPresent = Test-Path -PathType Leaf (Join-Path $Repo 'tools' 'codex-vm.exe')", ScRaw "$qemuPresent = [bool]$script:FallbackVmBin", ScBlank, ScRaw "if (-not $codexVmPresent -or -not $qemuPresent) {", ScRaw "    $missing = if (-not $codexVmPresent) { 'codex-vm' } else { 'qemu' }", ScRaw "    if (-not $Quiet) {", ScRaw "        Write-Host \"  vm-differential: SKIP (only one VM host on this machine; $missing missing)\"", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    exit 0", ScRaw "}", ScBlank, ScRaw "$work = Join-Path ([System.IO.Path]::GetTempPath()) \"vmdiff-$PID\"", ScRaw "New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $work | Out-Null", ScRaw "$compile = Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'compile.ps1'", ScBlank, ScRaw "# The QEMU arm runs FIRST, deliberately. It is the arm that can hang, and", ScRaw "# paying for the trusted compile before discovering that is waste.", ScRaw "function Invoke-Arm {", ScRaw "    param([string]$Name, [string]$HostVal)", ScRaw "    $cdx = Join-Path $work \"$Name.cdx\"", ScRaw "    $log = Join-Path $work \"$Name.log\"", ScRaw "    $prev = $env:CODEX_VM_HOST", ScRaw "    $env:CODEX_VM_HOST = $HostVal", ScRaw "    try {", ScRaw "        $sw = [System.Diagnostics.Stopwatch]::StartNew()", ScRaw "        & pwsh -NoProfile -File $compile -Src $Src -Out $cdx -Log $log -Kernel $Kernel *> $null", ScRaw "        $code = $LASTEXITCODE", ScRaw "        $sw.Stop()", ScRaw "    } finally {", ScRaw "        $env:CODEX_VM_HOST = $prev", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    if ($code -ne 0 -or -not (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $cdx)) {", ScRaw "        return @{ Ok = $false; Name = $Name; Code = $code }", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    return @{", ScRaw "        Ok = $true", ScRaw "        Name = $Name", ScRaw "        Cdx = (Get-FileHash $cdx -Algorithm SHA256).Hash", ScRaw "        Map = if (Test-Path \"$cdx.map\") { (Get-FileHash \"$cdx.map\" -Algorithm SHA256).Hash } else { '' }", ScRaw "        Seconds = [int]$sw.Elapsed.TotalSeconds", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "}", ScBlank, ScRaw "# RETRY ONCE, AND ONLY FOR AN ARM THAT PRODUCED NO BINARY (red, ruled", ScRaw "# 2026-08-31). A host that fell over is worth one more attempt. Two hosts", ScRaw "# that DISAGREE are never retried: a mismatch is the finding this check", ScRaw "# exists to report, and retrying it would launder a real disagreement into", ScRaw "# a pass on the second roll.", ScRaw "function Invoke-ArmOnceRetried {", ScRaw "    param([string]$Name, [string]$HostVal)", ScRaw "    $first = Invoke-Arm -Name $Name -HostVal $HostVal", ScRaw "    if ($first.Ok) { return $first }", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"  vm-differential: the $Name arm produced no binary (exit $($first.Code)), retrying once\"", ScRaw "    return Invoke-Arm -Name $Name -HostVal $HostVal", ScRaw "}", ScBlank, ScRaw "$qemu = Invoke-ArmOnceRetried -Name 'qemu' -HostVal 'qemu'", ScRaw "if (-not $qemu.Ok) {", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"  vm-differential: FAIL (the qemu arm did not produce a binary, exit $($qemu.Code))\"", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"      Detail: CODEX_VM_HOST=qemu pwsh build/compile.ps1 -Src $Src -Out out.cdx -Log out.log -Kernel $Kernel\"", ScRaw "    exit 1", ScRaw "}", ScBlank, ScRaw "$cvm = Invoke-ArmOnceRetried -Name 'codexvm' -HostVal ''", ScRaw "if (-not $cvm.Ok) {", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"  vm-differential: FAIL (the codex-vm arm did not produce a binary, exit $($cvm.Code))\"", ScRaw "    exit 1", ScRaw "}", ScBlank, ScRaw "if ($qemu.Cdx -ne $cvm.Cdx) {", ScRaw "    Write-Host '  vm-differential: MISMATCH -- the two VM hosts disagree on the compiler output'", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"      source:  $Src\"", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"      kernel:  $Kernel\"", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"      qemu:    $($qemu.Cdx)  [$($script:FallbackVmBin)]\"", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"      codexvm: $($cvm.Cdx)\"", ScRaw "    Write-Host '      One of these two hosts is not running the program it was given. Keep'", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"      the artifacts in $work and do not delete them.\"", ScRaw "    exit 1", ScRaw "}", ScBlank, ScRaw "if ($qemu.Map -ne $cvm.Map) {", ScRaw "    Write-Host '  vm-differential: MISMATCH -- binaries agree but the .map sidecars differ'", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"      qemu:    $($qemu.Map)\"", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"      codexvm: $($cvm.Map)\"", ScRaw "    exit 1", ScRaw "}", ScBlank, ScRaw "Remove-Item -Recurse -Force $work -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue", ScRaw "if (-not $Quiet) {", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"  vm-differential: OK (both hosts agree, $($qemu.Cdx.Substring(0, 16)), qemu $($qemu.Seconds)s / codex-vm $($cvm.Seconds)s)\"", ScRaw "}", ScRaw "exit 0"]

Section: The one stage

 TWO GUESTS, NEVER AT ONCE: the qemu arm runs to completion, then the codex-vm
 arm. Each arm may be retried once, so the stage can boot up to four guests in
 sequence and never two together.

  vmdiff-stage : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "compile through both hosts and compare", ps-why = "two independent VM hosts agreeing byte for byte carries information that an expired Authenticode signature cannot; one sample, not a proof", ps-in = ["Src", "Kernel", "Quiet"], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [PrGuests 1, PrKernel (SeVar "Kernel")], ps-verdict = [PoExit 0 "only one VM host is installed on this machine, so the check SKIPPED and reported success; a zero that means the check did not run", PoExit 1 "the qemu arm produced no binary, twice", PoExit 1 "the codex-vm arm produced no binary, twice", PoExit 1 "the two hosts disagree on the compiler output; one of them is not running the program it was given, and the artifacts are kept", PoExit 1 "the binaries agree and the .map sidecars do not", PoExit 0 "both hosts produced the same bytes"], ps-body = s01 }

Section: Assembly

  vmdiff-pipe : Pipeline = Pipeline { pl-name = "check-vm-differential", pl-doc = "Compile one source through BOTH VM hosts and compare the bytes", pl-params = vmdiff-params, pl-stages = [vmdiff-stage] }

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (emit-powershell (pipeline-to-shell vmdiff-pipe))
  end

